WEBVTT

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.119
Hi there.

00:00:11.119 --> 00:00:15.919
Welcome to this video where we are going
to learn what a digital footprint is.

00:00:16.799 --> 00:00:21.391
A digital footprint is the trail of data
you leave behind when you go online.

00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:25.519
Understanding footprints helps
you protect your privacy.

00:00:26.351 --> 00:00:28.639
The goal of this video is to explain

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:31.839
how digital footprints 
are created and why they matter.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.071
We will look at actions that leave traces,

00:00:35.071 --> 00:00:38.879
including actions you choose and actions
that happen in the background.

00:00:39.551 --> 00:00:42.559
Then we will practice ways
to leave a smaller footprint.

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:48.959
Imagine walking on a beach

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:51.967
and leaving footprints in the sand.

00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:56.511
Online you can also leave footprints,
but you cannot always see them.

00:00:57.151 --> 00:01:00.879
Your digital footprint is made
from your clicks, taps, and choices.

00:01:01.391 --> 00:01:03.759
Some footprints are created on purpose.

00:01:03.759 --> 00:01:06.959
For example,
posting a photo, writing a comment,

00:01:07.039 --> 00:01:10.031
liking a video, or sharing a message.

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:13.951
These actions can be seen 
by other people depending on your settings.

00:01:14.671 --> 00:01:17.679
Other footprints are created
quietly in the background.

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:20.591
Websites and apps 
can record what you click,

00:01:20.591 --> 00:01:23.599
how long you stay on a page
and what you search for.

00:01:24.031 --> 00:01:27.039
This can happen
even if you never post anything.

00:01:27.231 --> 00:01:30.479
Things that can be tracked
include pages you visit, buttons

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.679
you press, your device type,
and sometimes your location.

00:01:34.639 --> 00:01:38.399
Apps may also track which videos 
you watch and what you buy or look at.

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:42.031
This data helps services
learn what you might do next.

00:01:42.879 --> 00:01:45.871
Many companies track footprints 
to personalize content.

00:01:45.951 --> 00:01:48.991
They may show adverts
based on what you watched or searched for.

00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:52.431
They may also suggest
games, videos or products

00:01:52.431 --> 00:01:55.439
they think you will like.

00:01:59.087 --> 00:02:03.087
Footprints matter
because data can last a long time.

00:02:03.135 --> 00:02:06.143
If too much data is collected,
it can reveal patterns about you,

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:09.343
your interests, routines, and habits.

00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:13.103
The more data that exists,
the more careful you need to be.

00:02:13.823 --> 00:02:15.983
Oversharing makes footprints bigger.

00:02:15.983 --> 00:02:17.375
Sharing your name, school,

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:21.183
or location can make it easier
for strangers to identify you.

00:02:22.015 --> 00:02:24.415
Even photos can reveal private details

00:02:24.415 --> 00:02:27.503
in the background,
like a school sign or a home address.

00:02:33.087 --> 00:02:36.095
Here are simple ways 
to leave a smaller footprint.

00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:39.295
First, share less personal information,

00:02:39.295 --> 00:02:42.254
especially in games and sign up forms.

00:02:42.254 --> 00:02:45.246
If something is not needed,
do not give it.

00:02:46.254 --> 00:02:48.606
Second, log out when you are finished,

00:02:48.606 --> 00:02:51.614
especially on shared devices.

00:02:52.078 --> 00:02:53.750
Third, use privacy settings

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.686
like "only friends"
instead of "public".

00:02:57.278 --> 00:03:02.398
Privacy settings are like doors and curtains 
that control who can see your data.

00:03:02.398 --> 00:03:06.078
If you do not understand
a setting, ask a trusted adult to help.

00:03:06.766 --> 00:03:08.238
Trusted adults can help you.

00:03:08.238 --> 00:03:11.198
Check app permissions and privacy options.

00:03:11.198 --> 00:03:17.518
Asking for help is part 
of being a smart and safe digital citizen.

00:03:19.118 --> 00:03:20.622
Let's recap.

00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:24.014
A digital footprint is 
the trail of data you leave online.

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:28.238
Some footprints are active
and some are passive.

00:03:28.702 --> 00:03:32.270
Smaller footprints usually mean
better privacy and more control.

00:03:33.102 --> 00:03:34.862
Great work!

00:03:34.862 --> 00:03:38.862
In this video, you learned what a digital
footprint is and how it is created.

00:03:39.742 --> 00:03:41.310
Thank you for watching.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:44.158
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.